  <!-- THE GOLDEN RULE -->
  <section id="rule">
    <div class="eyebrow">The Foundation</div>
    <h2>The One Rule That<br/><em>Explains Everything</em></h2>
    <p>Every skincare layering question — what goes first, what goes last, can I mix these — is answered by one principle: <strong>thinnest texture to thickest, and water-based before oil-based.</strong></p>
    <p>This matters because thicker products physically block thinner ones from absorbing. If you put moisturizer before your serum, your serum sits on top of the moisturizer barrier and never reaches your skin. You're essentially applying an expensive product to a cream — not to your face.</p>

    <div class="rule-card">
      <div class="rc-label">🏆 The Golden Rule</div>
      <h3>Thin → Thick · Water → Oil · Active → Passive</h3>
      <p>Apply your lightest, most water-like products first. Work toward thicker creams and oils last. Treatments and actives always go before moisturizer so they can penetrate. SPF is always the absolute final step in the morning — nothing goes over it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pullquote">"Skincare order isn't arbitrary. It's physics. Thicker molecules physically block thinner ones from reaching your skin cells."</div>

    <div class="order-matters">
      <div class="om-card wrong">
        <div class="om-label">❌ Wrong Order Result</div>
        <h4>Products can't absorb properly</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Serum applied after moisturizer</li>
          <li>Active ingredients blocked by cream barrier</li>
          <li>SPF applied before moisturizer</li>
          <li>Vitamin C applied on dry unwashed skin</li>
          <li>Oil applied before water-based serum</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="om-card right">
        <div class="om-label">✅ Correct Order Result</div>
        <h4>Maximum ingredient absorption</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Cleanser preps skin for everything after</li>
          <li>Serums penetrate to deeper skin layers</li>
          <li>Moisturizer seals all actives in</li>
          <li>SPF sits on top and stays effective</li>
          <li>Every product does its actual job</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- AM ROUTINE -->
  <section id="amroutine">
    <div class="eyebrow">Morning Routine</div>
    <h2>The Complete <em>AM Sequence</em></h2>
    <p>Your morning routine focuses on protection and prevention — fighting the UV damage, pollution, and free radicals you'll encounter throughout the day. Every step builds toward that final layer of SPF.</p>

    <div class="step-list" style="border-radius:16px;margin-top:20px">

      <div class="step-item">
        <div class="step-num-col">
          <div class="step-circle c1">1</div>
          <div class="step-emoji">🫧</div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <div class="step-meta">
            <span class="step-name">Cleanser</span>
            <span class="step-timing timing-both">AM + PM</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-rule">⏱ Wait time: none — go straight to next step</div>
          <p class="step-desc">Start every routine on completely clean skin. In the morning, a gentle rinse or light cleanser removes overnight sweat, sebum buildup, and whatever was on your pillow. Cleansing first ensures every product you apply after actually reaches your skin — not a layer of overnight oil.</p>
          <div class="step-products">
            <span class="prod-chip">CeraVe Foaming (Oily)</span>
            <span class="prod-chip">CeraVe Hydrating (Dry)</span>
            <span class="prod-chip">Vanicream Gentle (Sensitive)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-tip">💡 AM tip: If your skin isn't oily overnight, a plain water rinse works fine. Save your cleanser for PM when you're removing sunscreen and pollution.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <div class="step-num-col">
          <div class="step-circle c2">2</div>
          <div class="step-emoji">💦</div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <div class="step-meta">
            <span class="step-name">Toner</span>
            <span class="step-timing timing-both">AM + PM</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-rule">⏱ Wait time: 30 seconds — let it absorb</div>
          <p class="step-desc">Modern toners are not the harsh, alcohol-based astringents of the 90s. A good toner restores your skin's pH after cleansing (which slightly disrupts it), adds a first layer of hydration, and prepares your skin to absorb everything that comes after. Think of it as priming a canvas before painting.</p>
          <div class="step-products">
            <span class="prod-chip">Some By Mi AHA/BHA Toner</span>
            <span class="prod-chip">Thayers Witch Hazel Toner</span>
            <span class="prod-chip">Paula's Choice BHA Liquid</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-tip">💡 Skip if minimalist: Toner is optional if you're doing a 4-step routine. Cleanser → Serum is perfectly fine for beginners.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <div class="step-num-col">
          <div class="step-circle c3">3</div>
          <div class="step-emoji">✨</div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <div class="step-meta">
            <span class="step-name">Essence</span>
            <span class="step-timing timing-both">AM + PM</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-rule">⏱ Wait time: 30 seconds — pat and move on</div>
          <p class="step-desc">An essence is a lightweight, water-like fluid that delivers concentrated hydration and skin-enhancing actives at a texture thinner than a serum. It's a K-beauty staple — and genuinely optional for most routines. If you use one, it goes after toner and before serum. Pat in gently — don't rub.</p>
          <div class="step-products">
            <span class="prod-chip">COSRX Snail Mucin Essence</span>
            <span class="prod-chip">SK-II Facial Treatment Essence</span>
            <span class="prod-chip">Missha Time Revolution Essence</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-tip">💡 Completely optional: Most people skip this step — especially in a budget routine. Add it only when you want to enhance hydration beyond what your serum delivers.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <div class="step-num-col">
          <div class="step-circle c4">4</div>
          <div class="step-emoji">🍊</div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <div class="step-meta">
            <span class="step-name">Serum</span>
            <span class="step-timing timing-both">AM + PM</span>
