          <p class="step-desc">Same logic as AM — restore pH, add hydration, prep skin for actives. If you're using an exfoliating toner (AHA/BHA), this is the time to use it — at night only, never in the morning. Chemical exfoliants increase photosensitivity so they should always be PM actives.</p>
          <div class="step-products">
            <span class="prod-chip">Paula's Choice BHA (PM only)</span>
            <span class="prod-chip">The Ordinary Glycolic 7% (PM only)</span>
            <span class="prod-chip">Thayers Witch Hazel (AM or PM)</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <div class="step-num-col">
          <div class="step-circle c4">3</div>
          <div class="step-emoji">🌙</div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <div class="step-meta">
            <span class="step-name">Treatment Serum (Retinol / Peptides)</span>
            <span class="step-timing timing-pm">PM Only</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-rule">⏱ Wait time: 20–30 minutes for Retinol (important)</div>
          <p class="step-desc">This is where night routines earn their power. Retinol accelerates cell turnover, stimulates collagen, and fades dark spots faster than almost any other topical ingredient. Peptides repair and rebuild. Both need to be PM-only — Retinol degrades in sunlight and increases UV sensitivity. The 20-30 minute wait before moisturizer reduces irritation for beginners.</p>
          <div class="step-products">
            <span class="prod-chip">The Ordinary Retinol 0.5% (Beginners)</span>
            <span class="prod-chip">CeraVe Retinol Serum (Sensitive)</span>
            <span class="prod-chip">TO Buffet Peptide Serum (All types)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-tip">💡 Retinol beginner tip: Start 2x per week for first month. Increase to every other night in month 2. Daily use from month 3 onward. Rushing causes peeling and irritation.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <div class="step-num-col">
          <div class="step-circle c5">4</div>
          <div class="step-emoji">👁️</div>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
          <div class="step-meta">
            <span class="step-name">Eye Cream</span>
            <span class="step-timing timing-both">AM + PM</span>
          </div>
          <div class="step-rule">⏱ Wait time: none</div>
          <p class="step-desc">PM is actually the more important time for eye cream — your skin repairs overnight and an eye treatment with peptides or retinol alternative (retinyl palmitate) delivers results while you sleep. Apply before moisturizer, tap gently with ring finger, and let it absorb.</p>
